ongside Ann Murray. \"He's been working on the road with Ann Murray and Andy Williams.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Ongoing History Introduces you to: \"History of the 90's\"","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6O5TCTO-go4"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Waco Standoff Playlist","body":"Andy Williams's songs were part of the playlist used to bombard the Branch Davidian cult compound in Waco, Texas, in 1993. This tactic was an attempt to break the will of David Koresh and his followers during their prolonged standoff with law enforcement. \"That playlist included AQ Breaking Heart by Billy Ray Cyrus, Nancy Sinatra, these boots are made for Wacan, some chanting by Tibetan monks, songs by Andy Williams, and some Christmas sing-alongs by Mitch Miller from the 1950s.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Using Music as a Weapon","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R1wdsGt07Gg"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Ellis Island Medal of Honor","body":"Won.","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5365910"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"star on Hollywood Walk of Fame","body":"Won.","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q17985761"}]}],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"These Boots Are Made for Walkin' (1966)","body":null,"year":1966,"extra":{"from":"Nancy Sinatra","from_id":252331481316855,"type":"song"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Using Music as a Weapon","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R1wdsGt07Gg"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Achy Breaky Heart (1992)","body":null,"year":1992,"extra":{"from":"Billy Ray Cyrus","from_id":153218094122684,"type":"song"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Using Music as a Weapon","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R1wdsGt07Gg"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Early Career and Influences","body":"He was a young comedian who worked frequently at The Improv Los Angeles and toured on the road with Ann Murray and Andy Williams. He gained notoriety after appearing on The Tonight Show with Johnny Carson, where his act was built on observations about \"the madness of life's idiosyncrasies.\" \"Here is a young comedian who works frequently at the improvisation Los Angeles, and he's been working on the road with Ann Murray and Andy Williams.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Jerry Seinfeld","from_id":73816729698226,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Ongoing History Introduces you to: \"History of the 90's\"","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6O5TCTO-go4"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Touring with Jerry Seinfeld","body":"As a young comedian, Jerry Seinfeld worked on the road with Ann Murray, alongside Andy Williams. \"He's been working on the road with Ann Murray and Andy Williams.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Ann Murray","from_id":70863134437929,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Ongoing History Introduces you to: \"History of the 90's\"","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6O5TCTO-go4"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Waco Standoff Playlist","body":"Mitch Miller's Christmas sing-alongs from the 1950s were part of the loud music bombardment directed at the Branch Davidian cult compound in Waco, Texas, in 1993. This was an attempt to psychologically pressure David Koresh and his followers during a 51-day standoff. \"That playlist included AQ Breaking Heart by Billy Ray Cyrus, Nancy Sinatra, these boots are made for Wacan, some chanting by Tibetan monks, songs by Andy Williams, and some Christmas sing-alongs by Mitch Miller from the 1950s.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Mitch Miller","from_id":189361941778067,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":